## Difference Between Primary Key Index and Unique Index in Oracle

| Feature                | Primary Key Index                                   | Unique Index                                      |
|------------------------|-----------------------------------------------------|---------------------------------------------------|
| Creation               | Automatically created with a `PRIMARY KEY` constraint | Created with a `UNIQUE` constraint or manually    |
| Uniqueness             | Enforces uniqueness                                 | Enforces uniqueness                               |
| NULLs Allowed          | **NOT NULL** enforced                               | Allows multiple `NULL` values                     |
| Number per Table       | Only one per table                                  | Multiple unique indexes allowed                   |
| Index Type             | Always unique                                       | Always unique                                     |

**Summary:**  
A primary key index enforces both uniqueness and `NOT NULL`, while a unique index enforces only uniqueness (and allows `NULL` values).
